  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The diagram shows two equipotential surfaces, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span>, in the gravitational field of a planet.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The gravitational potential at surface <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"-50 \\text{ MJ kg}^{-1}\"></span> and the gravitational potential at surface <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"-20 \\text{ MJ kg}^{-1}\"></span>. How much work is required to move a <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.0 \\text{ kg}\"></span> mass from surface <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> to surface <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span>?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"30 \\text{ MJ}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"60 \\text{ MJ}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"70 \\text{ MJ}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"140 \\text{ MJ}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
